#. Tag: para
#: acquireimages.docbook:22
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The Kipi acquire images plugin is a tool to scan images using a flat scanner."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: keyword
#: acquireimages.docbook:28
#, no-c-format
msgid "<keyword>KDE</keyword>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: keyword
#: acquireimages.docbook:29
#, no-c-format
msgid "Kipi"
msgstr "Kipi"

#. Tag: title
#: acquireimages.docbook:36
#, no-c-format
msgid "Acquire Images"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: acquireimages.docbook:38
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This plugin can be used to scan images using a flat scanner. The plugin uses "
"libksane, a &kde; interface for SANE library to control flat scanners."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: acquireimages.docbook:40
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"It can save images in all the formats supported by &kde;. For example the "
"following formats:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: acquireimages.docbook:43
#, no-c-format
msgid "png (8 and 16 bits per color)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: acquireimages.docbook:46
#, no-c-format
msgid "jpeg, jpg, jpeg 2000"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: acquireimages.docbook:49
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>bmp</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: acquireimages.docbook:55
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can check the status of your scanner support from the SANE project "
"website "
"by entering the information on this search page: <ulink "
"url=\"http://www.sane-project.org/cgi-bin/driver.pl\">"
"http://www.sane-project.org/cgi-bin/driver.pl</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: acquireimages.docbook:58
#, no-c-format
msgid "Scanner Selection"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: acquireimages.docbook:59
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If the selected scanner cannot be opened or if no default scanner is "
"provided, "
"a scanner selection dialog is opened."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: acquireimages.docbook:61
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The user can choose the scanner to be used and press <guibutton>OK</guibutton>"
" "
"to open the scanner. Pressing <guibutton>Cancel</guibutton> "
"will cause the plugin to exit."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: acquireimages.docbook:66
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>No scanner found</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: acquireimages.docbook:72
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>No scanner found</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: acquireimages.docbook:77
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In case no devices were found, maybe because the scanner is not plugged in or "
"switched off, correct that. Then the <guibutton>Reload device list</guibutton>"
" "
"can be used to reload the list of scanners."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: acquireimages.docbook:81
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Not all drivers/backends support this feature. In that case quit the plugin, "
"connect your scanner and restart the application."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: acquireimages.docbook:88
#, no-c-format
msgid "Main Window"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: acquireimages.docbook:90
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>Main window</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: acquireimages.docbook:96
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Main window</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: acquireimages.docbook:101
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the main window, the user has two sets of scan options: <guilabel>"
"Basic Options</guilabel> and <guilabel>Scanner Specific Options</guilabel>"
". The <guilabel>Basic Options</guilabel> tab contains the most common "
"parameters that the SANE scanner backends provide, while the <guilabel>"
"Scanner Specific Options</guilabel> tab contains all the options of the "
"backend. The options listed here depend on SANE support for your driver: "
"libksane (which the plugin uses) should be able to display most of the types "
"of "
"parameters that SANE provides (analog gamma tables are not supported at this "
"time)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: acquireimages.docbook:106
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>Scanner Specific Options tab</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: acquireimages.docbook:112
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Scanner Specific Options tab</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: acquireimages.docbook:117
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The scanner specific options contains more detailed options of the backends. "
"The plugin does not have any special handling for these options."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: acquireimages.docbook:121
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you are satisfied with your settings, you can use the little arrow on the "
"top of the options splitter. When clicked it collapses or expands the "
"options. "
"The collapser can overlap the preview area, but fades away when the mouse "
"cursor moves out of the collapser."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: acquireimages.docbook:127
#, no-c-format
msgid "Scanning"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: acquireimages.docbook:128
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To scan an image, the user can start with a preview scan and then select the "
"part of the scan area to do the final scan on. The preview scan is started by "
"pressing the preview button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: acquireimages.docbook:133
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>The Preview Button</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: acquireimages.docbook:139
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>The Preview Button</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: acquireimages.docbook:144
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When the preview is scanned the area for the final image can be selected."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: acquireimages.docbook:148
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>Selection and zoom</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: acquireimages.docbook:154
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Selection and zoom</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: acquireimages.docbook:158
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To better select the image the user can zoom in, out, to the current "
"selection "
"or zoom to fit the whole preview to the window."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: acquireimages.docbook:162
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>The \"zoom to fit\" button</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: acquireimages.docbook:168
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>The \"zoom to fit\" button</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: acquireimages.docbook:173
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When the image is selected the final image can be acquired by pressing the "
"final scan button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: acquireimages.docbook:178
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>The final scan button</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: acquireimages.docbook:184
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>The final scan button</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: acquireimages.docbook:189
#, no-c-format
msgid "You will see the progress of the scan."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: acquireimages.docbook:193
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>Scanning in progress</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: acquireimages.docbook:199
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Scanning in progress</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: acquireimages.docbook:206
#, no-c-format
msgid "Scanning Multiple Selections"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: acquireimages.docbook:207
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Sometimes you need only certain parts of an image. Instead of scanning the "
"whole picture and then using a graphics application (&eg; &kolourpaint;) to "
"save the different image parts into separate files, use the plugins multiple "
"selection feature."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: acquireimages.docbook:214
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>Multiple Selections</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: acquireimages.docbook:220
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Multiple Selections</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: acquireimages.docbook:224
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Scan a preview and then use the &LMB; to select the first part of the image "
"in "
"the preview. Hover the selected area with mouse cursor and click on the green "
"<guiicon>+</guiicon> icon to select the area. Selected areas are indicated by "
"a "
"red border. Now select the next parts of the image in the same way."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: acquireimages.docbook:228
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To remove a single selection hover the area with the mouse cursor and click "
"on "
"the red <guiicon>-</guiicon> icon. With <guilabel>Clear Selections</guilabel> "
"from the context menu launched with the &RMB; all selections in a preview can "
"be removed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: acquireimages.docbook:232
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you placed two separate images or photos on you scanner and started a "
"preview the plugin automatically preselect the different areas."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: acquireimages.docbook:235
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you are satisfied with your choice starting the final batch scan of all "
"selections. The selected parts of the image are scanned and saved separately "
"into different files."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: acquireimages.docbook:241
#, no-c-format
msgid "Help and Close"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: acquireimages.docbook:242
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"At the bottom of the main window you find the <guibutton>Help</guibutton> "
"and <guibutton>Close</guibutton> buttons."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: acquireimages.docbook:245
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guibutton>Help</guibutton> button brings up the menu described in the "
"section <ulink url=\"help:/fundamentals/ui.html#menus-help\">Help Menu</ulink>"
" "
"of the &kde; Fundamentals. The <guibutton>Close</guibutton> "
"button is used to exit the plugin."
msgstr ""

